        <h2>12 Answers Doctors Ask Us About Website + Online Booking + WhatsApp</h2>
        <p class="lede">Analysis based on ITD GrowthLabs' work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. Client names + case study details shared on discovery call under NDA.</p>

          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Does a cosmetic surgery clinic in Mumbai really need a website in 2026?</h3>
            <div>Yes — but a modern one, not a brochure. Modern cosmetic and plastic surgery practice website essentials in 2026: (1) mobile-first + Core Web Vitals green, (2) integrated online booking, (3) WhatsApp Cloud API chat, (4) before-after gallery (compliance-safe), (5) doctor + team profiles, (6) Google reviews embed, (7) location + directions with local schema, (8) blog for SEO + AI Overview visibility. 60-80% of first patient discovery happens via Google or Instagram, and your website converts that intent to a booking.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How much does a cosmetic surgery clinic website cost?</h3>
            <div>Modern cosmetic and plastic surgery practice website in 2026: Rs 60,000 - Rs 4,00,000 depending on complexity. Solo clinic single-page + booking + WhatsApp: Rs 60K-1.2L. 2-3 doctor multi-page + blog + gallery: Rs 1.5-2.5L. Multi-location with per-location pages + advanced booking: Rs 2.5-4L. Enterprise hospital with patient portal + telemedicine: Rs 5-25L. ITD includes website in Enterprise retainer or one-time build at cost.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What online booking system should a cosmetic surgery clinic use?</h3>
            <div>Top options for Cosmetic + Plastic Surgery in Mumbai: (1) Practo — largest patient network + reviews + booking (SaaS Rs 5-25K/mo), (2) Cliniify — solid booking + EMR integration (Rs 3-8K/mo), (3) SetMore or Calendly for simple booking (Rs 500-2K/mo), (4) custom booking on your website via WordPress plugin or headless calendar API (one-time Rs 30-80K + Rs 2-5K/mo). Practo drives most patient discovery in Mumbai; own-site booking maximizes brand + margin.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you integrate WhatsApp Cloud API for a cosmetic surgery clinic?</h3>
            <div>ITD's WhatsApp Cloud API setup for cosmetic and plastic surgery practices: (1) Meta Business Manager verified WhatsApp Business Platform account, (2) Interakt or AiSensy as messaging platform (Rs 4-15K/mo), (3) welcome + qualifying + booking + reminder + follow-up flows, (4) opt-in template messages for outbound, (5) 15-min response SLA business hours, (6) inside-sales escalation for high-AOV, (7) CRM integration (LeadSquared / Zoho / HubSpot). Setup time 2-3 weeks.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you set up online booking + WhatsApp integration seamlessly?</h3>
            <div>Standard integration for Cosmetic + Plastic Surgery: Website booking form → CRM (Zoho/HubSpot/LeadSquared) → WhatsApp Cloud API auto-message → SMS + email confirmation → Google Calendar booking → 24hr reminder → post-visit review request. Fallback path if patient exits booking: WhatsApp abandoned-booking recovery flow. Full pipeline setup 3-4 weeks + Rs 40K-1.5L one-time.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Should we use Practo or our own website booking for cosmetic surgery?</h3>
            <div>Best strategy: use BOTH. Practo captures patient discovery searches (60-70% of new patient discovery in Mumbai still starts on Practo for cosmetic surgery). Own-website booking captures brand-search + direct + social + ad-driven bookings + eliminates Practo commission. Split typically 40-60% Practo, 60-40% own-website + walk-ins + referrals at maturity.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What Core Web Vitals matter for cosmetic surgery clinic websites?</h3>
            <div>Google + AI Overview ranking requires green Core Web Vitals. Targets for cosmetic and plastic surgery practices: (1) Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) < 2.5s, (2) Interaction to Next Paint (INP) < 200ms, (3) Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) < 0.1. Common fixes: image compression + WebP conversion, lazy loading, remove third-party bloat (heavy chat widgets, unused analytics), server-side caching + CDN. Green CWVs improve organic ranking 15-40%.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Do we need a blog on our cosmetic surgery clinic website?</h3>
            <div>Yes — blog is the #1 driver of long-tail SEO + AI Overview visibility for cosmetic and plastic surgery practices. Target: 40-100 educational articles covering every top patient question in cosmetic surgery. Each article ranks Google + gets cited in ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude AI Overviews when patients ask about cosmetic surgeon, plastic surgeon, rhinoplasty, facelift, liposuction, breast surgery, mommy makeover. ROI compounds: month 1-6 = building, month 7-12 = organic traffic scales 3-8x, month 12+ = 30-50% of new inquiries from organic search.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD build websites for cosmetic surgery clinics?</h3>
            <div>ITD website build workflow: (1) Discovery + brand + competitive audit (Week 1), (2) UX + wireframe + copy (Week 2-3), (3) Design + brand + assets (Week 3-4), (4) Development + booking + WhatsApp + CRM (Week 4-7), (5) On-site photography + testimonials (Week 5-6), (6) QA + Core Web Vitals + accessibility (Week 7-8), (7) Launch + SEO + IndexNow + analytics (Week 8). Total 6-10 weeks.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What content should a cosmetic surgery clinic website include?</h3>
            <div>Essential pages: (1) Home with clear value + services + doctor credentials, (2) About + doctor profiles, (3) Services (one page per major treatment/procedure), (4) Before-after gallery (compliance-safe), (5) Blog for SEO, (6) Reviews + testimonials, (7) Booking + contact + directions, (8) Locations (if multi-location), (9) Insurance + fees (transparent = trust), (10) Patient education library.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you migrate an existing cosmetic surgery website without losing SEO?</h3>
            <div>ITD migration workflow: (1) Full crawl + rank + traffic + backlink audit before migration, (2) 1:1 URL redirect map (301) preserving link equity, (3) content parity check (no ranking-page content removed), (4) new schema + AI Overview optimization, (5) sitemap resubmission + IndexNow ping + GSC re-verification, (6) 8-week post-launch rank monitoring, (7) rollback plan if rank drops >20%. Typical rank impact +5% to +20% within 90 days.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD maintain a cosmetic surgery clinic website over time?</h3>
            <div>Included in Growth+ retainers: (1) monthly content + blog updates (4-8 new pieces), (2) security + plugin patching, (3) Core Web Vitals monthly review, (4) A/B testing on high-traffic pages (hero + booking + services), (5) schema + AI Overview keyword tracking, (6) 3-monthly SEO audit + gap-fill, (7) backup + monitoring + uptime SLA. Enterprise tier adds custom feature development.</div>
